  4. User Products and Installation Information.

  A "User Product" is either (a) a "consumer product", which means any
tangible personal property which is normally used for personal, family,
or household purposes, or (b) anything designed or sold for
incorporation into a dwelling.  In determining whether a product is a
User Product, doubtful cases are resolved in favor of it being a
User Product.  For a User Product, "Installation Information" means
any methods, procedures, authorization codes, etc., required to install
and execute modified versions of the covered work in that User Product
from a copy of the Corresponding Source.  The requirement to provide
Installation Information does not apply if you or a third party
conveys the object code in, or embodied in, a User Product, and the
object code is never used in a User Product, or the covered work is
not a User Product.

